  <section>
    <h2>The editor</h2>
    <p>DubaiPoints is, at launch, a single-editor publication using the organisational byline <strong>DubaiPoints Editorial</strong>. The editor is a UAE resident who has used UAE-issued credit cards, transferred a salary to a UAE bank, and redeemed Skywards and Etihad Guest miles personally. The editor's name is not currently published, so we do not describe this as a named byline. Published card figures are sourced, dated and subject to editorial verification; unresolved fields are withheld or marked pending.</p>
    <p>If contributors join later, individual bylines and relevant experience will be published when those contributors choose public attribution.</p>
    <p>For editorial questions, corrections, or tips: <a href="mailto:info@dubaipoints.ae">info@dubaipoints.ae</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where we live</h2>
    <p>DubaiPoints is written from the UAE. That matters because the products we cover are sold in the UAE, the eligibility rules we report on are enforced by UAE banks, and the redemption sweet spots we track are checked against actual UAE-departure availability. We do not parachute international templates into UAE coverage — and we do not import US or UK financial assumptions that don't apply here.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we don't claim to be</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Regulated financial advisers.</strong> We are not authorised by the DFSA or the UAE Central Bank to provide personalised financial advice, and we do not.</li>
      <li><strong>Tax advisers, immigration advisers, or legal advisers.</strong> Where our coverage touches these areas — for example, residency requirements for credit cards, or salary-band tax treatment for expats — we report what the bank or government has published and recommend that readers consult a qualified specialist for their personal situation.</li>
      <li><strong>A complete database.</strong> We cover the cards, programmes, and offers we have been able to verify. Where a bank or product is not yet on the site, that absence is not a verdict — it is queue order.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>All published work follows the standards laid out in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>: independence from commercial relationships, source-faithful units, sourced and dated verification, and an age flag when a card's verification is more than 90 days old. Funding sources are described in <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how we make money</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>One inbox at launch: <a href="mailto:info@dubaipoints.ae">info@dubaipoints.ae</a>. Editorial questions, corrections, tips, and commercial enquiries all route there. As the team grows we'll publish dedicated addresses; until then, please mark the subject line so it gets to the right reader (e.g. "Correction:", "Tip:", "Partnership:"). Commercial enquiries have no influence on editorial coverage — see <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how we make money</a>.</p>
  </section>

